  "package": "html/template",
  "notes": "html/template: contextual autoescaping is a port of Go's escaper (context, transition, escape, js, css, url, html). Typed content types are newtypes converting to named template values; errors are TemplateError::Escape(Error) with Go's ErrorCode values and messages. Escaper edits go to a copy of the parse tree, so call Template::tree after the first execution. An unvalidated MarshalJSON result is compacted but only syntax-checked with Go's scanner messages; strings are UTF-8.",
